# Website Assessment (WA)

When the user requests a WA (Website Assessment) using `/wa [URL]`, follow these steps:

## Instructions

1. **Read the template** at `docs/TEMPLATE.md` for the exact format and sections
2. **Read domain knowledge** at `docs/DOMAIN_KNOWLEDGE.md` for Global-e specific rules and app support matrix
3. **Navigate to the provided URL** and systematically assess the site following the playbook workflow
4. **Complete all sections** of the template with proper status labels (✅ Verified, ❔ Unconfirmed, ❌ Absent)
5. **Always output the completed WA directly in chat** (see Output Format below). Do not only save it to a file or summarize that it was saved.
6. **Save to file** at `logs/assessments/YYYY-MM-DD_domain_WA.md`

## Output Format (CRITICAL)

**ALWAYS return the completed assessment directly in chat as PLAIN TEXT - not inside markdown code blocks and not only as a file preview.**

**The saved file at `logs/assessments/YYYY-MM-DD_domain_WA.md` must be identical to the chat output.**

Rules for output:
- First line must be exactly `Website Assessment` (no `#` heading)
- Section titles are plain text on their own line (no `#`, `###`, bold, or suffixes like `(DETAILED)`)
- Do NOT wrap the assessment in triple backticks (```)
- Do NOT use markdown link syntax like `[text](url)` - use plain URLs only
- Do NOT use em dashes in WA output. Use a plain hyphen separator instead.
- Do NOT use horizontal rules (`---`) in completed WA output
- DO use only these status labels on line items: `✅ Verified`, `❔ Unconfirmed`, `❌ Absent`
- DO put warnings in the detail text, not in custom status labels like `⚠️ Verified`
- DO put the line item subject first, bolded, then the status marker and label, then the evidence/detail.
- Preferred bullet format: `• **Subject** - ✅ Verified - Evidence or finding here.`
- DO keep this subject-first format for every WA line item unless the user explicitly asks for a different format.
- DO use plain bullet points and line breaks
- DO put one blank line between every bullet line item for Jira/Confluence copy-paste spacing
- DO keep shipping and returns under `Shipping & Logistics` (no separate top-level Returns section)
- DO use internationalization headers like `Market 1 (United States, USD)` followed by the six standard bullets with status labels
- DO use `Takeaway: one sentence` at the end of sections that need a summary
- DO read `docs/TEMPLATE.md` section `0) Output Requirements` for the full canonical format and section order before writing any WA
- The user must be able to select all the text and copy it directly into Jira/Confluence with formatting intact

Example of CORRECT output format:
```
# Website Assessment

Merchant Overview

• **Brand** - ✅ Verified - Example Brand
• **Primary URL** - ✅ Verified - https://example.com
• **Other Locales / Sites** - ❔ Unconfirmed - https://example.co.uk, https://example.eu

Evidence Log (Working Links)

• **Home** - ✅ Verified - https://example.com
• **PDP example** - ✅ Verified - https://example.com/products/widget
• **Cart** - ✅ Verified - https://example.com/cart
...
```

Example of WRONG output (do NOT do this):
- Wrapping everything in a code block
- Using `[Cart](https://example.com/cart)` instead of plain URL
- Only saving to file without showing in chat

## Key Requirements

- **Navigate, don't guess:** Always use the site's own navigation (header menus, footer links, buttons) to discover pages. Never hardcode or guess URLs - follow the actual links on the page
- Label every line as **✅ Verified**, **❔ Unconfirmed**, or **❌ Absent**
- Use **plain URLs** (not markdown links) for easy Jira copy-paste
- Mark deductions with **[Inference]**
- Flag Global-e red flags when present: Smile.io, Recharge, DG products, etc.
- Do NOT add default “Smile.io absent” or “Recharge absent” bullets. Only mention Smile.io or Recharge if they are actually detected or directly relevant to a finding.
- Don't purchase - step through checkout as far as allowed
- Test 2-3 international markets if possible
- Capture screenshots for key findings

## Section Order

1. Merchant Overview
2. Evidence Log (Working Links)
3. Platform & Site Structure
4. Catalog & Products
5. Checkout & Payments
6. Shipping & Logistics
7. Loyalty, Subscriptions, and CRM
8. Internationalization Testing
9. Legal and Compliance (surface-level)
10. Business Restrictions (split)
11. Apps, Integrations, and Data Layer (visible only)
12. Jewelry Merchant Considerations (Presales Scoping) - optional, jewelry merchants only
13. Tech Risks and Integration Notes (Presales)
14. Opportunities and Recommendations
15. Open Questions
16. Next Steps
17. Appendix - Screens and Notes

## Example Usage

User: "/wa https://example.com"
User: "Can you do a WA for https://example.com"